  "term": "valproic acid",
  "definition": "Valproic acid is a fatty acid medication with anticonvulsant and anti-manic effects, used to treat epilepsy and bipolar disorder. Its therapeutic action is not fully understood, but it may work by raising gamma-aminobutyric acid levels in the brain or changing voltage-gated sodium channel function.",
